 "claim_summary": "Holder A opens mkvterm on a not-activated partition with a sealed stdin pipe (hmcpctl's _SealedStdin) and later closes the pipe's write end, so the HMC sees stdin EOF. Arm `single`/`single-fast`: A alone; about 10.1-10.5 s after EOF A receives ' The write socket has closed. Exiting.\\n', its stream ends and mkvterm exits 0, and a probe C (a fresh mkvterm on an independent connection) then acquires while A's SSH connection is still open; in `single-fast` a probe started 1 s after EOF found the vterm still held. Arms `takeover`, `race`, `eof-first`: client B takes the vterm (ConsoleSession(take_over=True), or a bare rmvterm then ConsoleSession) and A sends EOF after B holds, between B's rmvterm and B's mkvterm, or 2 s before B's takeover. A exits the same way, B's stream stays open and silent for 10 s after A's exit, C finds the vterm held, and B's own close proves release. Every run starts and ends with the partition Not Activated and the console slot free (baseline, restore-check probes).",
